<title>JAPAN: IBJ lead-manages syndicate loan for Chinese plants.</title>
<headline>IBJ lead-manages syndicate loan for Chinese plants.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-07-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Industrial Bank of Japan (IBJ) Ltd will lead-manage two syndicate loans for Chinese petrochemical plants, a bank spokesman said on Thursday.</p>
<p>IBJ is acting as a co-arranger for a $60 million syndicated loan to a project in Tianjin by an affiliate of a Korean conglomerate. Some eight banks, including Singapore and Korean banks, were involved in the five-year loans.</p>
<p>The IBJ, along with Sanwa Bank Ltd and two others, will also lead-manage the loan worth of $100 million to the Chinese government-owned petrochemical project in Guangdong.</p>
<p>The eight-year loan was raised from Asian banks.</p>
</text>
